WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.710
-There's a word missing.
-What?

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.780
-It's missing?
-Yes.

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.780
I wonder why nobody's noticed until now.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:17.020
Sasaki-san, please check the vocabulary
list just in case.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.550
Okay.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.160
"Chishio" is on the list like it should be.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.530
Let's insert "chishio"
and adjust the number of columns.

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:38.140
My big concern here is if
there are other missing words....

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:46.050
Stop everything we have been doing.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:49.280
We are going to restart the fourth draft
from the beginning.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:54.750
Let's check all 240,000 words
one more time.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.340
The Great Passage

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.140
A quiet dreamlike morning
The madder red sky

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:15.640
Shines through the window
And reflects on my pen

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:21.820
The vivid clatter of the night,
I wander between cities like a cat

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:24.650
Deep thoughts, flexible conception

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:28.390
Foreseeable aspirations
Distant memories; unruly hair

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:34.830
Narrow mind, large circle of friends;
long silence, short greeting; tone of voice

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:38.260
The light in our eyes
That differ from each other

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.400
Traces of friendship
That’s not in the treaty

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:47.670
In the ocean that sweeps
The sand of eternity

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:54.750
Swept and sunk in the waves with sparse
opposites and similarities

00:01:55.180 --> 00:02:01.220
Clashing and exact opposites become
resolved and connected

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:02.790
Reference, conclusion

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:07.790
I’ll gather words that have
Scattered over many months and years

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.900
The fragrant sea breeze

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:14.200
The connection that rests on the seashore
Become one.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:28.380
Pride

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:35.490
What we're asking you to do
is extremely vital for Daitokai.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.560
I'd like you to keep that in mind
while you work.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:46.200
Team, this is going to be
quite an undertaking.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:49.300
But no matter how many days it takes,

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.170
it's something we must do.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:55.610
Please, I need your help to ensure

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:58.950
Daitokai is not a ship with any holes.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:06.290
All right, let's get started then.

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:14.590
We're making sure the words
on this list

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:17.600
have all been entered
in the proof sheet properly.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.230
Okay, I understand.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:22.500
Progress Chart

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:32.680
You've already done that much?

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:34.950
How can I increase my pace?

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.350
Don't talk to me right now.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:46.990
Oh, I'll get it.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:50.930
Yes, this is Genbu Book's
Dictionary Editorial Department.

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:53.500
Oh, hello.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.510
Yes, one moment please.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.310
-Majime-san.
-Yes?

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:06.280
It's Matsumoto-sensei's wife.

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:10.320
Apparently, he's in the hospital.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:11.880
Which hospital?

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:23.030
Sakazaki Hospital

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:28.470
Araki-san is getting the room number.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:33.440
I have noticed that he's lost some weight
recently.

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:39.010
I heard you hired some temps to go over
the fourth draft one more time.

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:40.550
Yes.

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:43.550
Majime, is it going to be all right?

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:46.690
It will be fine.

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:52.530
I thought so.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:53.990
He's in room 203.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:55.960
-Does the sensei know?
-No.

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:57.960
Probably best not to tell him.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:01.330
We don't want anything distracting him
from his health.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.540
-Yes.
-All right, let's go.

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:13.380
-Yes.
-Pardon me.

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:21.420
-Oh, look who's here.
-Sensei.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:24.620
I'm sorry. I know you must all be busy.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.090
It is nice to see you again.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:29.060
These are the sensei's favorites.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.900
Oh, thank you so much.

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:33.600
That's very considerate.

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:36.800
I'm so sorry you've had to come
all this way.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.640
Please, don't mention it.
How are you feeling?

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:42.440
Oh, I'm doing pretty well considering.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:47.610
No, sensei! You can't push yourself
too hard.

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:51.480
I think my wife overreacted
when she called you.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:55.460
I'm only here to get some tests.

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:59.490
But this is a good opportunity for you
to take things slow.

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:04.100
But we are so close to being finished.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:07.100
It's so disappointing.

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:11.600
How is Daitokai coming along?

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:13.970
It's coming along great!

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:17.510
I heard you almost got the book binding
designed?

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:18.680
Yes.

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:24.380
Is that so?
I am looking forward to seeing it.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:28.420
In any case, I can't believe you're still
collecting vocabulary words

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:30.520
so soon after being hospitalized!

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:34.060
It's part of my life now.

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:35.800
Of course it is!

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:38.160
I look forward to reading them later.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:42.900
Actually, I've run into some quite
interesting words.

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:48.780
How long do you believe
these tests will take?

00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:51.510
I actually don't know.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:54.710
I haven't even been told how many days
he'll be kept here.

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:56.550
I see.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:59.790
But sensei looked well enough.

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:03.920
We'd love to have him back
after a little R&R.

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:07.590
Yes.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:15.540
This might be a good opportunity
like you said, Araki-san.

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:20.010
As you can see, Matsumoto is a man
who doesn't know how to take a break.

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:21.440
Yes.

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:26.880
Please, don't worry about him
and just focus on your work.

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:30.850
I'm looking forward to Daitokai's
completion as well.

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:32.550
Thank you very much.

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:36.590
-But please, if you find out anything....
-Of course.

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:39.190
I will give you a call.

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:41.990
Thank you.

00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:43.900
Please take care.

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:15.080
Great. Could you take this next then?

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:17.320
I didn't know there were still so many left.

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:19.990
Don't worry. We're making progress.

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:23.820
But it's still pretty overwhelming, isn't it?

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:25.890
Don't let that bog you down.

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:28.860
-Let's just work hard.
-Okay.

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:56.260
Kugiri kikaku. Kuuki reikyaku. Kuuki gita.

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:59.630
Kuukikei. Kuukishitsu. Kuukisei.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:02.260
Kuukichoan. Kuuki densen.

00:09:02.590 --> 00:09:05.300
Kuukyo. Kuugyo. Gukyo.

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:08.030
Kukyo. Kuukiyo suito.

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:10.740
Guugin. Guuku.

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:11.660
-Oh, sorry.
-Good work today!

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:13.700
I've brought food!

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:16.000
Yeah!

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:19.070
Eat up! You too, Sasaki-san.

00:10:48.730 --> 00:10:51.400
I can't focus anymore.

00:10:51.740 --> 00:10:54.170
Take a break then!

00:10:54.310 --> 00:10:56.880
-Okay.
-Feels nice, doesn't it?

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:42.990
Okay, who asked for laundry?

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:45.390
Come on up one by one.

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:47.360
Okay, coming!

00:11:48.130 --> 00:11:50.260
How are you guys doing?

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:52.970
I've really picked up the pace.

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:54.200
Me too.

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:56.030
Everyone's gotten so much faster.

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:58.040
I'm super-fast now.

00:11:58.170 --> 00:11:59.170
Good.

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:00.810
Then I will allow you seconds.

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:03.910
-Yes!
-Thank you very much!

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:49.920
Majime.

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:53.330
The world is losing the words....

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:56.560
-Majime!
-It's no use.

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:00.430
Majime!

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:05.400
Yes?

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:08.510
We might be at our limit here.

00:13:08.840 --> 00:13:11.310
Some haven't been home in a while.

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:14.250
This is just dropping our productivity.

00:13:14.380 --> 00:13:16.250
You're right.

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:20.120
Let's send everyone home tonight to rest.

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:22.550
I think that'd be best.

00:13:58.390 --> 00:14:00.530
I'm home.

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:14.170
Hi there, Torao-san.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:16.640
Good morning.

00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:22.050
Welcome home.

00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:26.050
Good to be home.

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:42.100
Here you are.

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:56.620
I've missed your cooking.

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:59.320
-Are you getting enough to eat?
-Yes.

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:02.520
You have to make sure you're eating
properly.

00:15:02.720 --> 00:15:04.090
I know.

00:15:04.390 --> 00:15:07.130
-We still have more work to do.
-Okay.

00:15:09.530 --> 00:15:13.670
I went to visit Matsumoto-sensei
at the hospital yesterday.

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:15.500
And?

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:19.140
It seems he'll be discharged
over the weekend.

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:20.540
Thank goodness.

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:24.010
How was he doing?

00:15:24.140 --> 00:15:27.380
I don't know. He was smiling.

00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:31.380
But sometimes he'd look really tired.

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:33.120
I see.

00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:39.660
I wonder how old the sensei is.

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:44.530
He hasn't really visually aged
these last 14 years.

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:46.770
That's true.

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:50.100
I would believe it
if you told me he was 90.

00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:54.410
I'd also believe you if you told me
he's 68.

00:15:54.710 --> 00:15:56.040
That's true.

00:15:56.170 --> 00:15:59.040
Perhaps dedicating your life
to something

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:02.480
frees you from the world somehow.

00:16:06.050 --> 00:16:08.290
You know, that applies to you too,
Micchan.

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:11.220
You don't change either.

00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:17.260
You too.

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:22.370
You haven't changed since the first day
I met you.

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:34.110
-Good luck at work.
-Thank you.

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:41.290
How is it, Majime?

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:44.290
I think it's a very good design.

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:45.460
All right!

00:16:45.590 --> 00:16:48.190
This means the other departments
will go into action.

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:50.530
I look forward to your support.

00:16:50.660 --> 00:16:54.270
I thought you would enjoy it,
Majime-san.

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:57.500
It truly is wonderful.

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:24.600
I'm finished. There are no issues.

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:26.830
-Ye--
-Not yet.

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:31.740
No issues here either.

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:48.850
We are in the clear.

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:55.760
Which means we have finished
checking everything.

00:17:56.600 --> 00:18:00.170
Good work, everyone.

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:03.700
Yeah! It's over!

00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:09.240
Thank you. We did it.

00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:11.340
Thank you so much!

00:18:13.850 --> 00:18:16.350
Majime-san!

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:20.420
-A job well done!
-Yes, and you as well.

00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:24.690
At first, I thought it was really mundane.

00:18:24.820 --> 00:18:26.830
But it was actually fun.

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:28.560
Is that so?

00:18:28.690 --> 00:18:31.260
Please contact us
if you need any more help.

00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:32.830
Me too.

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:35.370
Of course.

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:36.640
Good work.

00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:38.700
Have a nice night.

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:40.670
I'm heading out now.

00:18:40.810 --> 00:18:42.770
Good luck with the rest.

00:18:42.910 --> 00:18:44.680
Thank you.

00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:51.550
We were truly blessed by a great staff.

00:18:51.680 --> 00:18:53.490
It's not over yet.

00:18:53.620 --> 00:18:55.920
-Yes.
-Good work!

00:18:56.760 --> 00:19:00.530
-Careful on your way home!
-Yes. Thank you!

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:02.960
Good work, all of you.

00:19:03.300 --> 00:19:05.360
I heard from one of the temps.

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:08.700
I heard there weren't
any other missing words.

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:11.200
That's great!

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:14.540
-It's proof that your hard--
-What, Nishioka?

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:17.810
You haven't been around at all lately,
so what do you want now?

00:19:17.940 --> 00:19:20.550
What? Oh, come on, Araki-san!

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:26.720
I've been working my butt off for Daitokai
in my own way.

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:29.650
I have the proof right here.

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:31.560
Ta-da!

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:33.830
It's Daitokai's new mascot.

00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:35.730
His name is Kai-kun!

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:41.430
Pretty cute, right?

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:43.840
Yes, so cute!

00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:45.770
What the heck is this?

00:19:45.900 --> 00:19:48.610
That's rather tasteful for you, Nishioka.

00:19:48.740 --> 00:19:52.910
Not you too, Sasaki-san!
You're all so mean!

00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:19.740
Pride: Honor
Pride in his/hers work

00:20:23.940 --> 00:20:26.580
Hey

00:20:26.710 --> 00:20:34.320
It’s a full moon tonight

00:20:35.390 --> 00:20:37.790
I speak to you

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:45.030
Softly as you sleep

00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:49.470
Your gestures

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:52.300
Attitude

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:57.340
And way of life

00:20:57.780 --> 00:21:03.980
Mean so much to me more than any word

00:21:04.350 --> 00:21:09.890
So please stay the way you are

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:15.830
I & I = You & I
Feel it

00:21:16.390 --> 00:21:21.530
Here with you, forever by your side

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:24.100
I’ve loved you

00:21:24.440 --> 00:21:29.410
From the day

00:21:29.540 --> 00:21:34.580
We met

00:21:42.920 --> 00:21:44.920
What a beautiful day.

00:21:45.060 --> 00:21:46.960
Grandma, sit right there.

00:21:47.090 --> 00:21:49.090
What's gotten into you?

00:21:49.430 --> 00:21:53.470
Let's take a picture of all of us.
Hurry up, Micchan.

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:55.070
Okay.
